<title>BELGIUM: BBL details costs of euro launch.</title>
<headline>BBL details costs of euro launch.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Bruxelles Lambert (BBL) said on Wednesday that the planned introduction of the euro, Europe's single currency, in 1999 would cost it a non-recurrent two billion francs.</p>
<p>BBL board chairman Jacques Moulaert told the annual shareholders meeting that an initial loss of profits from lost foreign exchange trade and the disappearance of the &quot;natural protection&quot; the bank gets from being in the Belgian franc zone was an estimated total of 3.7 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
